+/*
+ * surya (Poco X3 NFC), sweettouch=2: Novatek NT36672C TDDI on GENI SE0 in
+ * SPI mode (qupv3_se0_spi, 0x880000), CS0, SPI mode 0, 8-bit words, <= 8 MHz.
+ * Facts from surya's dtbo (fragment 62) and Xiaomi surya-q-oss nt36xxx_spi:
+ *  - SPI pins gpio49-52, function qup00 (2nd), WEST tile; ABL leaves them as
+ *    plain GPIOs, so they are muxed here (6 mA, no pull, as the DT active state).
+ *  - Touch reset TLMM gpio8, interrupt TLMM gpio9 (NORTH tile). The panel reset
+ *    is PM6150L GPIO 9, a different chip: gpio8 resets only the touch MCU.
+ *  - Power is shared with the panel (lab/ibb, L18A): nothing is voted here.
+ *    L11C, which the sweet driver votes, feeds the Wi-Fi RF on surya.
+ * Milestone 1: clocks, pins, SPI, bootloader reset, chip id read.
+ * Milestone 2: firmware download with the chip's hardware CRC
+ * (nvt_download_firmware_hw_crc, hw_crc = 2). The NT36672C keeps no firmware;
+ * Xiaomi's novatek_ts_huaxing_fw.bin is not redistributable, so it is not in
+ * this tree: a locally built ADT carries it as /surya-touch "firmware".
+ * Milestone 3: finger points read from the event buffer and logged.
+ * Milestone 4: the same points go to iOS through touch_report -> SweetHID.
+ */
